.TH LMARGIN 1.SH NAMElmargin \- indent text by a left margin.SH SYNOPSIS\fBlmargin\fR[\-l\fIn\fR] < infile > outfile.SH DESCRIPTION\fBlmargin\fRcopies the standard input to the standard output with\fIn\fRspaces in front of every line, five unless told:\fBlmargin \-l4 < notes\fRindents by four.  Its usage line says\fBepson\fRand speaks of a printer, which it inherited from the program it waswritten beside; it writes only to the standard output..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOepson, fmt, pep